<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Library Guide | Far Reach Co.</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Learn how the Far Reach Co. Library app works: scope, folders, uploads, search, bulk actions, and pack integration." />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/features/info.css" />
  <script src="/lib/MobileNavHandler.js" defer></script>
  <%- include('./partials/icons') %>
</head>
<%- include('./partials/google') %>

<body>
  <%- include('./partials/nav') %>
  <div class="container-fluid p-3 info-container">
    <div class="intro">
      <h1 class="text-center">Library Guide</h1>
      <p>How to use the Library app to organize images and prep assets for your tables and Wyrlds.</p>
      <small>
        <a href="/library-packs-guide">Library Packs Guide</a>
        |
        <a href="/vtt-guide">VTT Guide</a>
      </small>
      <hr>
    </div>

    <div class="quick-links" aria-label="Page sections">
      <a href="#scope">Library Scope</a>
      <a href="#layout">Page Layout</a>
      <a href="#images">Image Workflow</a>
      <a href="#folders">Folders</a>
      <a href="#bulk">Bulk Actions</a>
      <a href="#packs">Packs Integration</a>
      <a href="#permissions">Permissions</a>
      <a href="#tips">Practical Tips</a>
    </div>

    <section id="scope">
      <h2>Library Scope</h2>
      <p>The Library app supports two scopes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>My Library</strong> for personal assets (<code>/library</code>).</li>
        <li><strong>Wyrld Library</strong> for shared campaign assets (<code>/library?wyrld=&lt;id&gt;</code>).</li>
        <li>Wyrld Library requires Wyrld editor/manager access.</li>
        <li>The page title updates to show the active scope so you always know where actions apply.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="layout">
      <h2>Page Layout</h2>
      <figure class="toolshot-card toolshot-card--focus">
        <img
          src="/assets/screen_shots/library_screenshot.png"
          alt="Library app showing folder tree, search, and an image grid in a Wyrld library."
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>Library layout: sidebar controls on the left, scope context at top, and the asset grid in the main panel.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Sidebar:</strong> search, scope tabs, and creation actions.</li>
        <li><strong>Main panel:</strong> image grid or packs view depending on selected tab.</li>
        <li><strong>Header controls:</strong> sort mode, select toggle, and scope indicators.</li>
        <li>Library supports <strong>Images</strong> and <strong>Packs</strong> tabs. If packs are unavailable in the current scope, you will see a disabled Packs indicator.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="images">
      <h2>Image Workflow</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use <strong>Upload Image</strong> to queue one or many files.</li>
        <li>Incompatible files are filtered out automatically.</li>
        <li>Duplicate upload entries are skipped in queue handling.</li>
        <li>Search matches image name and notes.</li>
        <li>Sort options include newest, name, and size.</li>
        <li>Image detail modals support metadata editing and pack membership management.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="folders">
      <h2>Folders and Organization</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Create root folders or subfolders directly from the sidebar.</li>
        <li>Use <strong>All Images</strong>, <strong>Unsorted</strong>, or a specific folder in the folder tree.</li>
        <li>Deleting a folder moves images to the parent context instead of deleting images.</li>
        <li>Folder counts are shown per folder to speed up navigation.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="bulk">
      <h2>Bulk Actions</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Enable <strong>Select Multiple</strong> to choose many images from the grid.</li>
        <li>Selected images can be moved to folders in one operation.</li>
        <li>Selected images can be added to a pack in one operation.</li>
        <li>Selected images can be removed from the scope when cleanup is needed.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="packs">
      <h2>Packs Integration</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The Library app includes pack creation, discovery, install, and management flows.</li>
        <li>Packs are scoped the same way as images (user scope vs Wyrld scope).</li>
        <li>Discover mode lets you preview published packs before install.</li>
        <li>For full ownership/visibility/install behavior, use the <a href="/library-packs-guide">Library Packs Guide</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="permissions">
      <h2>Permissions and Access Rules</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Personal library actions require login.</li>
        <li>Wyrld library actions require Wyrld editor/manager permissions.</li>
        <li>Pack features are gated by plan scope:
          <strong>Pro User</strong> for personal scope and <strong>Pro Wyrld</strong> for Wyrld scope.</li>
        <li>Sandbox table mode limits pack discovery/install controls during table sessions.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="tips">
      <h2>Practical Tips</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Keep personal testing assets in My Library and publish reusable sets as packs.</li>
        <li>Use Wyrld Library for campaign-specific assets that your co-managers need.</li>
        <li>Tag packs consistently so discover search works better for your team.</li>
        <li>Use folder structure for broad organization, then search for fast retrieval during prep.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
  <%- include('./partials/footer') %>
</body>

</html>
